  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 221 AM MDT MON AUG 10 2026\nThe long-term period is looking to be more active (especially \nacross southwest Idaho). Monsoonal moisture will continue to \npush north through the end of the week, with LREF mean PWATs \nincreasing to around the 90th percentile of climatology. Come \nthursday afternoon, chances of showers and thunderstorms will \noverspread the majority of southwest Idaho and portions of \neastern Oregon, aided by the upper level trough and shortwave. \nModel soundings indicate elevated instability continuing into \nFriday morning, so some nocturnal thunderstorms can't be ruled \nout overnight Thursday. Showers and afternoon thunder will \ncontinue into the weekend, especially over the Central Idaho \nMountains and near the Nevada border. With atmospheric moisture \nincreasing, heavy rain will become more of a threat, especially \nover steep terrain and recently burned areas. Chances of showers\nand thunder will begin to taper off over the weekend as the \nshortwave exits our areas. This is barring higher terrain where \nisolated to scattered afternoon thunderstorms will remain. With \ngeneral troughing continuing near the west coast, an active \npattern could continue beyond the weekend. Temperatures will be \nwarm through the extended, but generally near normal, even \nleaning below normal by the end of the week.",
